    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0847" n="833" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg833"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7726: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-11T15:00:00+07:00">January 11, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. I called on Generalissimo this morning by appointment, accompanied by
                        Atcheson,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d613-f1"/> delivered message and found
                    occasion to make comments suggested (25, January 5, 5 p.m.). Kung was present,
                    acted as interpreter and translated message to Chiang. While Kung made some
                    deprecatory remarks to Generalissimo in regard to the Treasury recommendations,
                    they both received the message affably <pb facs="0848" n="834" xml:id="pg834"/>
                    and the Generalissimo thanked me for delivering it and indicated that after
                    study of it he would wish to make reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d613-f1" n="28" xml:id="d613-f1-content">
                <p>George Atcheson, Jr., Counselor of Embassy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
